UptoSettlementSettleTest
├── when payer authorization is missing
│   └── it should reject the settlement
├── when the current timestamp is before validAfter
│   └── it should return NotYetValid
├── when the current timestamp equals validAfter
│   └── it should allow settlement
├── when the current timestamp equals deadline
│   └── it should return Expired
├── when the current timestamp is after deadline
│   └── it should return Expired
├── when maxAmount is zero
│   └── it should return InvalidAmount
├── when maxAmount is negative
│   └── it should return InvalidAmount
├── when amount is negative
│   └── it should return InvalidAmount
├── when amount is greater than maxAmount
│   └── it should return InvalidAmount
├── when amount is zero
│   ├── when autoRevoke is true
│   │   ├── it should return zero
│   │   ├── it should leave token balances unchanged
│   │   └── it should clear the allowance
│   └── when autoRevoke is false
│       └── it should preserve the full allowance
├── when amount is between zero and maxAmount
│   ├── when autoRevoke is true
│   │   ├── it should transfer the requested amount
│   │   └── it should clear the remaining allowance
│   └── when autoRevoke is false
│       ├── it should transfer the requested amount
│       └── it should preserve the remaining allowance
├── when amount equals maxAmount
│   ├── when autoRevoke is true
│   │   └── it should transfer the maximum and leave no allowance
│   └── when autoRevoke is false
│       └── it should transfer the maximum and leave no allowance
├── given the payer is a G-account
│   └── it should record authorization for the G-account
├── given the payer is a C-account
│   └── it should record authorization for the C-account
└── when the partial-settlement authorization tree is recorded
    └── it should exclude amount and bind the root and approval arguments
